# Runtime target env for spring-on-exeris — Spring MVC + JPA running on the Exeris
# ingress in COMPATIBILITY mode (targets/exeris-spring-runtime-app-comp). Structural
# sibling of spring-runtime.env; the intended differences:
#
#   - Runner jar = the compat module's spring-benchmark-app jar, which boots the Exeris
#     kernel HTTP ingress + ExerisCompatDispatcher (ADR-011) instead of Tomcat. Same
#     Spring @RestController code, hosted on the Exeris runtime.
#   - Self-set port 9004 via EXERIS_PORT (app.properties maps exeris.runtime.network.port
#     from ${EXERIS_PORT}) so it can co-reside with spring-hibernate (9001) in the same
#     aggregate triad. Health probe target = :9004.
#   - JVM opts: SPRING_JAVA_OPTS carries the triad's iso-2048 Spring heap (1280m) + the
#     telemetry-off JFR overlay + NMT — IDENTICAL to spring-hibernate, so the
#     spring-hibernate vs spring-on-exeris pair is heap/diagnostics-fair (only the ingress
#     differs: Tomcat vs Exeris-compat). PLUS the embedded Exeris kernel's required
#     native-access flags (--add-opens sun.nio.ch/java.io, --enable-native-access,
#     --enable-preview) and -Dspring.classformat.ignore=true so Spring's classpath scan
#     tolerates the preview-marked (minor 0xFFFF) kernel classes.
#
# LABELLING (corrected 2026-08-20): this is a COMPATIBILITY target, which is a SEPARATION
# AXIS, not a confidentiality boundary. Rows must be labelled Community + Compatibility + H1,
# stored separately, and routed to the compat/ track; they must never be blended with
# pure-mode rows (native Exeris / Tomcat Spring / Quarkus) without the explicit compat caveat.
# They are PUBLISHABLE.
#
# This comment previously read "EXCLUDED from the public docs path ... published
# internal-only", citing CLAUDE.md's Enterprise-vs-public scoping. That is the exact
# over-application CLAUDE.md now calls out by name: spring-on-exeris is NOT excluded
# (corrected 2026-08-11), exeris-spring-runtime is a product repo listed separately from the
# enterprise repos and has never been confidential, and every spring-on-exeris* arm is
# tier=community in the pair manifest. The confidentiality rule covers raw JFR/diagnostics
# and Enterprise internals (H3, locality, enterprise targets) — not open-core arms that
# happen to sit on a labelling axis whose neighbour is Enterprise. CLAUDE.md records this
# same conflation happening twice before; this file was a third instance.

START_MODE=external
HEALTH_URL=http://localhost:9004/health
HEALTH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=90

EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL=${EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL:-jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/postgres?prepareThreshold=1}
EXERIS_DB_USERNAME=${EXERIS_DB_USERNAME:-postgres}
EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD=${EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD:-postgres}
EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE=${EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE:-16}
EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE=${EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE:-256}
SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT=${SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT:-9004}
SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY=${SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY:-}
SPRING_JAVA_OPTS=${SPRING_JAVA_OPTS:-}
EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST=${EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST:-localhost}
EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT=${EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT:-8124}
# Native-access + preview flags the embedded Exeris kernel needs; classformat.ignore lets
# Spring scan the preview-marked kernel classes. Appended AFTER SPRING_JAVA_OPTS so heap/JFR win.
EXERIS_NATIVE_JAVA_OPTS=${EXERIS_NATIVE_JAVA_OPTS:-'--add-opens java.base/sun.nio.ch=ALL-UNNAMED --add-opens java.base/java.io=ALL-UNNAMED --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED --enable-preview -Dspring.classformat.ignore=true'}
EXTERNAL_PID_FILE=${EXTERNAL_PID_FILE:-/tmp/exeris-${USER:-unknown}-spring-on-exeris.pid}

EXTERNAL_START_CMD='EXERIS_PORT="$SPRING_ON_EXERIS_PORT" EXERIS_HTTP_MAX_VERSION="${EXERIS_HTTP_MAX_VERSION:-HTTP_1_1}" EXERIS_HTTP_H2C_UPGRADE_ENABLED="${EXERIS_HTTP_H2C_UPGRADE_ENABLED:-false}" EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL="$EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL" EXERIS_DB_USERNAME="$EXERIS_DB_USERNAME" EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD="$EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD" EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE" EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE" SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL="$EXERIS_DB_JDBC_URL" SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME="$EXERIS_DB_USERNAME" SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD="$EXERIS_DB_PASSWORD" SPRING_DATASOURCE_HIKARI_MINIMUM_IDLE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MIN_SIZE" SPRING_DATASOURCE_HIKARI_MAXIMUM_POOL_SIZE="$EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE" EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST="$EXERIS_AXONSERVER_HOST" EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT="$EXERIS_AXONSERVER_PORT" ${SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY:+taskset -c ${SERVER_CPU_AFFINITY} }java $SPRING_JAVA_OPTS $EXERIS_NATIVE_JAVA_OPTS -jar targets/exeris-spring-runtime-app-comp/target/spring-benchmark-app-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar > /tmp/exeris-spring-on-exeris-9004.log 2>&1 & echo $! > "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE"'
EXTERNAL_STOP_CMD='if [[ -f "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE" ]]; then pid="$(cat "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE")"; kill "$pid" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; rm -f "$EXTERNAL_PID_FILE"; fi'

TARGET_TIER=community
TARGET_PROTOCOL=h1
COMPARISON_AXIS=within-tier-compat

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAGA ROSTER (e2e-shop-order-saga, CONTRACT-v2.2, added 2026-08-20)
#
# This env was written for the entity-read triad, where the arm co-resides with
# spring-hibernate. Three things MUST be reconciled before it can serve as a saga roster
# arm under spring_on_exeris_h1_park100_v3, and none of them is a version bump:
#
#   1. PORT COLLISION. 9004 is also restate's k6-facing facade port
#      (runtime/drivers/env/restate-runtime.env, health_url http://localhost:9004/health in
#      the asset matrix). The saga campaign runs both arms in one roster. One of them must
#      move; spring-on-exeris is the newcomer, so it moves.
#
#   2. POOL SIZE. EXERIS_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE defaults to 256 here against the saga roster's 32.
#      A pool eight times larger than every other arm's is not a fair row. The saga runner
#      exports the roster value, so verify it actually reaches this arm rather than assuming
#      the default is overridden.
#
#   3. --enable-preview. Carried because the old kernel line shipped preview-marked classes
#      (minor 0xFFFF) and Spring's classpath scan needed -Dspring.classformat.ignore=true to
#      tolerate them. exeris-community dropped both flags at kernel 0.11.0. Whether
#      exeris-spring-runtime 0.7.0 still needs them depends on the kernel line it pulls
#      transitively — check the built jar, do not assume either way.
#
# SAGA ELIGIBILITY IS THE OPEN QUESTION, NOT THE VERSION. The asset matrix records that this
# arm's saga terminal state does not resolve at all: flow steps run on kernel worker virtual
# threads outside the request-scoped compat provider binding, giving saga_success_rate=0.
# That is the same family of defect as the storage-context scope mismatch fixed in
# exeris-community on 2026-08-19. Until a run under spring_on_exeris_h1_park100_v3 resolves
# its sagas, the arm is "listed and pending" per CONTRACT-v2.2 §1 — it does not silently
# disappear from the roster table, and it does not appear in it as a measured row either.
